From: Daniel Delgado Ramos <328510259+thinkddr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:11:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: taps and the wheel through non modal overlays, and
 focus scopes

- An overlay that implements TapThrough() lets the click (glfw, on mouse down) or the
  tap (mobile) that dismisses it reach what it was covering: a menu, not a modal dialog.
- An overlay that implements ScrollThrough() lets the mouse wheel scroll what it covers,
  and is refreshed afterwards so it can follow what moved underneath.
- An object that implements FocusScope() restricts keyboard focus traversal to the
  subtree it returns: a navigation drawer that is not an overlay.
